course: dictionary
lesson: 12513
title: Where words come from
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Every word has a story. Its derivation is where it comes from and how it was made. Many English words are built from smaller parts, or borrowed from older languages such as Latin and Greek.
explain: You can build new words by adding a suffix to the end of a word. «Happiness» is derived from «happy» by adding -ness. The word «derive» becomes «derivation» when you add -ation.
explain: In maths and science, a derivation is a step-by-step working that shows how a rule or answer is reached. «The teacher showed the derivation of the formula on the board.» Each step follows from the one before it.
fact: Derivation means where a word comes from and how it was made.
fact: «Happiness» is derived from «happy» by adding the suffix -ness.
fact: Many English words are derived from Latin or Greek, such as «aquarium», from the Latin «aqua», meaning water.
fact: A suffix is a group of letters added to the end of a word to change its meaning or form.
fact: In maths, a derivation is a step-by-step working that shows how an answer is reached.
exercise: The word «happiness» is derived from which word? | *Happy | Hippo | Sad | Happen
exercise: «Aquarium» comes from the Latin word «aqua». What does aqua mean? | Air | Fish | Glass | *Water
exercise: In maths, what is a derivation? | A picture of a triangle | *A step-by-step working that shows how an answer is reached | A type of number | A quick guess
test: Which suffix turns «happy» into «happiness»? | -ly | *-ness | -ful
test: Which word is derived from «derive» by adding -ation? | Deriver | *Derivation | Derive it again
exam: Which sentence uses derivation to mean where a word comes from? | «The derivation of the puppy was a long sleep.» | «The derivation of my bike is very fast.» | *«The derivation of «pen» goes back to the Latin word «penna», meaning feather.»
